  "foaf:name": "Bridging UN Nutrition and Ocean Science Decades",
  "sdo:name": "Bridging UN Nutrition and Ocean Science Decades",
  "sdo:description": "Following the UN General Assembly’s extension of the Decade of Action on Nutrition to 2030, 2026 marks a pivotal moment to accelerate action and fully integrate aquatic foods into sustainable food systems. Through the initiative “Bridging the Decades,” the Global Action Network on Sustainable Food from the Oceans and Inland Waters, established by Norway in 2017 and extended to 2030, will mobilize coordinated activities linking the Nutrition Decade and the United Nations Decade of Ocean Science. This contribution will deliver events and collaborative initiatives, convening stakeholders across nutrition, fisheries, aquaculture, and ocean science to advance solutions for food security, improve access to safe and nutritious aquatic foods, and scale sustainable impact from healthy waters to healthy people. Creating actions in support of for sustainable aquatic food systems for healthy diets supporting as well as ensuring the role of the ocean for nourishing the global population.",
